From 7174fa95eeea6eb3ec2656beca4c8ae5cdeb3b9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:17:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/28] iomap: simplify direct io validity check

JIRA: https://issues.redhat.com/browse/RHEL-XXXXX

commit 7eac331869575d81eaa2dd68b19e7468f8fa93cb
Author: Keith Busch <kbusch@kernel.org>
Date:   Wed, 27 Aug 2025 07:12:55 -0700

    The block layer checks all the segments for validity later, so no need
    for an early check. Just reduce it to a simple position and total length
    check, and defer the more invasive segment checks to the block layer.

    Signed-off-by: Keith Busch <kbusch@kernel.org>
    Reviewed-by: Hannes Reinecke <hare@suse.de>
    Reviewed-by: Martin K. Petersen <martin.petersen@oracle.com>
    Reviewed-by: Christoph Hellwig <hch@lst.de>
    Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>

Conflicts: RHEL 9 spells the block size check (1 << blkbits) - 1
    instead of bdev_logical_block_size(iomap->bdev) - 1; only the
    bdev_iter_is_aligned() call is removed.

Signed-off-by: Showta Ishizaki <zakinko@snowrabbit.org>
---
 fs/iomap/direct-io.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fs/iomap/direct-io.c b/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
index 9c33806fa..ee7185aa5 100644
--- a/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
+++ b/fs/iomap/direct-io.c
@@ -281,8 +281,7 @@ static loff_t iomap_dio_bio_iter(const struct iomap_iter *iter,
 	size_t copied = 0;
 	size_t orig_count;
 
-	if ((pos | length) & ((1 << blkbits) - 1) ||
-	    !bdev_iter_is_aligned(iomap->bdev, dio->submit.iter))
+	if ((pos | length) & ((1 << blkbits) - 1))
 		return -EINVAL;
 
 	if (iomap->type == IOMAP_UNWRITTEN) {
-- 
2.55.0

